  "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nIntegrate Megatron FSDP v2 with Transformer Engine partial CUDA Graph capture and validate end-to-end MoE training through the ordinary module execution path. Capture suspends owned FSDP execution hooks and retains existing BF16 compute buffers. Replay enters `nn.Module.__call__()` so hooks refresh current weights and preserve gather/reduction ordering. Reshard invalidates readiness while keeping graph addresses stable. The graph helper snapshots mutable RNG state for rollback and resets graphs before releasing retained buffers.\n\n## Scope and dependencies\n\nBF16 without symmetric memory, fixed shapes, TP=PP=CP=1, ZeRO-1/2/3, EP and gradient accumulation. Partial capture covers attention, dense MLP, router and router-paired preprocess, with representative GPT/Hybrid, attention/MLA and grouped/shared-expert combinations. Dynamic token dispatch/combine, routed experts, FSDP communication and optimizer remain eager; EP preprocess may capture routing-count metadata gathers. Whole-layer capture, FP8/FP4, recomputation, TP/PP/CP expansion and the dedicated EP-overlap schedule are outside scope.\n\nDepends on #9372 and #9374; both fixes are excluded from this diff. Validation uses [composed source a8a8424](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/commit/a8a842466016426769ca479eac22a6354e4668a4), including the prerequisites. Normal-path evidence uses PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130 and unmodified TE 2.20.2.\n\n## Correctness and failure recovery\n\nAll [28 focused cases](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/tree/4c50d26554c39dcdab59e4bc6552b9f643a8557a/mfsdp-v2-core-split-20261112/reduced-tests-20261112) pass per rank on two PRO GPUs: model/scope combinations, ZeRO modes, communication streams, numerical/optimizer parity, dropout/RNG, evaluation, capture failure cleanup, deletion and checkpoint/recapture. [Four-GPU tests](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/tree/c9d6469a76afdcf36e5428cc826cae4b708af15b/mfsdp-v2-core-split-20261112) cover EP2/expert-DP2.\n\nStock `pretrain_gpt.py` trains a **2.09B GPT MoE proxy on WikiText-103**: 16 layers, hidden 2048, 16 experts/top-8, BF16/ZeRO-3, sequence 1024, microbatch 1, GA2, dropout 0.1; graph scopes `attn moe_router moe_preprocess`. All 45 per-rank losses match exactly across eager/graph benchmark repeats within each topology, with no skipped steps. Separate EP2 runs compare complete logical local-shard snapshots at steps 4/12: parameters, main weights and Adam state are byte-identical. Gradients are numerically identical; one expert gradient has 4756 signed-zero differences (`−0.0` versus `+0.0`), with maximum absolute difference 0 and matching zero-normalized hashes.\n\nMCore-owned preparation/finalization failures are tested for cleanup and retry. Stock TE 2.20.2 warmup exceptions can leave temporary hooks; independent [NVIDIA/TransformerEngine#3862](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3862) supplies cleanup and passes focused TE plus two-rank GPT/Hybrid MoE retry checks using isolated Python overlays. That fix is required for the tested TE-warmup retry path, not normal training. Arbitrary exception recovery and fatal CUDA/NCCL errors are outside the guarantee.\n\n## Event attribution and preserved concurrency\n\nA four-A6000 EP2/expert-DP2 trace matches **132 readiness event chains/rank**, links all **64 graph launches/rank** to their current-unit waits, and records **32 successor-prefetch/graph intersections/rank**. Actual target units and DeviceMesh dimensions distinguish ordinary DP, expert DP and EP. Expert-DP AG and RS overlap graph compute; ordinary-DP AG/RS and EP token A2A have zero intersection in this recording. Preprocess count-gathers inside graphs are separately attributed; no FSDP parameter AG is captured. The shared fourth GPU is used for ordering/concurrency evidence only.\n\nOn three idle A6000s, a measurement-only control serializes graph replay against FSDP streams without changing model work, buffers or capture scope. Three runs average **2733.70 ms/step**, versus **2598.32 ms** normally (**4.95% less time relative to the control**); trace intersections disappear. A same-count empty-stream placebo retains intersections and takes **2586.51 ms/step**, with comparable CPU enqueue overhead (~3 ms/step). All losses match. This establishes a bounded scheduling benefit, not an exact hidden-network-time measurement.\n\n## Steady performance and memory\n\nEach eager/graph mode has three separate 45-step runs on idle A6000s, timing steps 16–45 without profiling or hashing. Time is the mean of the slowest rank's window average; memory is the maximum per-rank steady peak across repeats.\n\n| Topology | Eager → graph time | Eager → graph peak allocated / reserved |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 GPUs, EP2/expert-DP1, batch 4 | 1178.77 → 1024.31 ms; **−13.10% step time / +15.08% throughput** | 21.720 / 23.814 → 20.495 / 25.391 GiB |\n| 3 GPUs, EP1/expert-DP3, batch 6 | 2584.68 → 2598.32 ms; **+0.53% step time** | 16.354 / 17.801 → 15.124 / 19.402 GiB |\n\nMax-rank capture-helper setup spans 2.325–2.916 s (EP2) and 2.103–2.349 s (EP1). Retained non-alias compute storage is **32.074 MiB × 16 units = 513.188 MiB/rank**, following FSDP ownership; this is residency, not peak-memory growth. Graph-private pools and allocator caching also matter; external CUDA/NCCL allocations are excluded. The previous graph OOM under a 17.360 GiB budget remains a capacity limitation; successful runs above use adequate headroom.\n\nResults are specific to the proxy and topology. EP dispatch/combine overlap, full OLMoE, long-run convergence and general scaling remain unqualified. Full upstream CI is pending. [Evidence bundle](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/tree/c8883d7b176494c59a7f32ef585f655471bcff11/mfsdp-v2-core-split-20261112/gap-closure-20261113): exact commands, software/data hashes, per-rank reports, event inputs/analysis and recorded timeline. Design RFC: #9113; original roadmap: #6757.\n\n## Code provenance\n\nNo code copied or adapted from external repositories. Reuses Megatron FSDP/RNG helpers and TE's existing graph API.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] Relevant unit tests and usage documentation accompany the implementation.\n- [ ] Registered functional-test recipe added; manual real-text validation is recorded above.\n- [x] Formatter and lint pipeline checked against the already-fetched base.\n- [x] Kernel determinism coverage checker passes; no numerical kernel is added.\n",
